d to its red anchor.\n0031: \n0032:     Rule:\n0033:     - Use the top-left quadrant's motif as the source pattern.\n0034:     - For each other quadrant, scale the motif by the ratio of that quadrant's red block size to the source red block size.\n0035:     - Reflect horizontally for right-side quadrants, vertically for bottom quadrants (both for bottom-right).\n0036:     - Align the scaled/reflected motif so its red region overlaps the target anchor, then stamp non-bg pixels.\n0037: \n0038:     Key insight: Red block size encodes the scale factor; quadrant position encodes the reflection axes.\n0039:     \"\"\"\n0040:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\n0041:     h, w = g.shape\n0042:     out = g.copy()\n0043: \n0044:     bg = get_bg(g)\n0045:     mid_r, mid_c = _find_dividers(g, bg)\n0046: \n0047:     # Find red anchor blocks (color 2) in each quadrant.\n0048:     red = components_mask(g == 2, connectivity=4)\n0049:     assert red, \"grid must contain red (color 2) anchor blocks\"\n0050: \n0051:     # Quadrant key: (top/bottom, left/right)\n0052:     anchors: dict[tuple[int, int], tuple[int, int, int]] = {}\n0053:     # value: (r0,c0,size)\n0054:     for pts in red:\n0055:         r0, c0, r1, c1 = bbox_coords(pts)\n0056:         rr = (r0 + r1) // 2\n0057:         cc = (c0 + c1) // 2\n0058:         qb = 0 if rr < mid_r else 1\n0059:         qr = 0 if cc < mid_c else 1\n0060:         size = max(r1 - r0 + 1, c1 - c0 + 1)\n0061:         key = (qb, qr)\n0062:         assert key not in anchors, \"each quadrant must contain exactly one red anchor block\"\n0063:         anchors[key] = (int(r0), int(c0), int(size))\n0064: \n0065:     assert (0, 0) in anchors, \"top-left quadrant must contain a red anchor block\"\n0066:     sr0, sc0, sL = anchors[(0, 0)]\n0067:     assert sL > 0, \"top-left red anchor must have positive size\"\n0068: \n0069:     # Build a source patch around the TL motif: take the non-bg connected component (4-neigh)\n0070:     # in the TL quadrant that contains the TL red anchor.\n0071:     tl = g[0:mid_r, 0:mid_c]\n0072:     comps = components_mask(tl != bg, connectivity=4)\n0073:     patch_bb = None\n0074:     for pts in comps:\n0075:         # component contains any red pixel?\n0076:         if any(tl[r, c] == 2 for r, c in pts):\n0077:             r0, c0, r1, c1 = bbox_coords(pts)\n0078:             patch_bb = (int(r0), int(c0), int(r1), int(c1))\n0079:             break\n0080:     assert patch_bb is not None, \"top-left quadrant must contain a non-bg component with a red pixel\"\n0081: \n0082:     pr0, pc0, pr1, pc1 = patch_bb\n0083:     patch = tl[pr0 : pr1 + 1, pc0 : pc1 + 1].copy()\n0084: \n0085:     def resize_nn(img: np.ndarray, new_h: int, new_w: int) -> np.ndarray:\n0086:         src_h, src_w = img.shape\n0087:         if new_h <= 0 or new_w <= 0:\n0088:             return img.copy()\n0089:         rr = (np.floor(np.arange(new_h) * src_h / new_h)).astype(int)\n0090:         cc = (np.floor(np.arange(new_w) * src_w / new_w)).astype(int)\n0091:         rr = np.clip(rr, 0, src_h - 1)\n0092:         cc = np.clip(cc, 0, src_w - 1)\n0093:         return img[rr[:, None], cc[None, :]]\n0094: \n0095:     # For each quadrant anchor, paste a scaled/reflected version of the patch.\n0096:     for (qb, qr), (tr0, tc0, tL) in anchors.items():\n0097:         if (qb, qr) == (0, 0):\n0098:             continue\n0099:         patch_t = patch\n0100:         if qr == 1:\n0101:             patch_t = np.fliplr(patch_t)\n0102:         if qb == 1:\n0103:             patch_t = np.flipud(patch_t)\n0104: \n0105:         ratio = float(tL) / float(sL)\n0106:         new_h = int(round(patch_t.shape[0] * ratio))\n0107:         new_w = int(round(patch_t.shape[1] * ratio))\n0108:         new_h = max(1, new_h)\n0109:         new_w = max(1, new_w)\n0110:         patch_s = resize_nn(patch_t, new_h, new_w)\n0111:         roundtrip = resize_nn(patch_s, patch_t.shape[0], patch_t.shape[1])\n0112:         assert np.array_equal(roundtrip, patch_t), \"scaling must preserve all motif information\"\n0113: \n0114:         # Align scaled red bbox in patch_s to the target red bbox.\n0115:         rr_red, cc_red = np.where(patch_s == 2)\n0116:         assert rr_red.size > 0, \"scaled source patch must contain red anchor pixels\"\n0117:         ar0, ac0 = int(rr_red.min()), int(cc_red.min())\n0118:         place_r0 = tr0 - ar0\n0119:         place_c0 = tc0 - ac0\n0120: \n0121:         rr_p, cc_p = np.where(patch_s != bg)\n0122:         for rr0, cc0 in zip(rr_p.tolist(), cc_p.tolist(), strict=False):\n0123:             val = int(patch_s[rr0, cc0])\n0124:             rr_t = place_r0 + rr0\n0125:             cc_t = place_c0 + cc0\n0126:             if not (0 <= rr_t < h and 0 <= cc_t < w):\n0127:                 continue\n0128:             if rr_t == mid_r or cc_t == mid_c:\n0129:                 continue\n0130:             if out[rr_t, cc_t] == 2:\n0131:                 continue\n0132:             out[rr_t, cc_t] = val\n0133: \n0134:     return out\n0135: \n0136: # --------------- generator (o5x) ---------------\n0137: \n0138: # --- Grid constants ---\n0139: BG = 4                  # background color\n0140: DIV = 1                 # divider color\n0141: RED = 2                 # anchor color\n0142: GRID_SIZE = 27          # full grid dimension\n0143: MID = 13                # divider row/col index\n0144: QUADS = {               # (row_lo, row_hi, col_lo, col_hi) inclusive per quadrant\n0145:     (0, 0): (0, 12, 0, 12),\n0146:     (0, 1): (0, 12, 14, 26),\n0147:     (1, 0): (14, 26, 0, 12),\n0148:     (1, 1): (14, 26, 14, 26),\n0149: }\n0150: \n0151: # --- Source motif parameters ---\n0152: SOURCE_ANCHOR_SIZE = 2                  # TL anchor is always 2x2\n0153: BLOCK_DIMS = [(2, 2), (2, 3), (3, 2), (3, 3)]  # logical block sizes for block method\n0154: BLOCK_PROB = 0.5                        # prob of block method when not forced\n0155: FILL_RATIO_MIN = 0.5                    # minimum motif fill ratio\n0156: FILL_RATIO_MAX = 0.8                    # maximum motif fill ratio\n0157: FREEFORM_H_RANGE = (3, 6)              # freeform motif height range\n0158: FREEFORM_W_RANGE = (3, 6)              # freeform motif width range\n0159: MOTIF_COLORS_MIN = 3                    # min distinct non-bg colors (including red)\n0160: MOTIF_COLORS_MAX = 5                    # max distinct non-bg colors\n0161: COLOR_POOL = [0, 1, 3, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9]  # non-red, non-bg candidate colors\n0162: \n0163: # --- Target anchor parameters ---\n...\n0361:         q_r0, q_r1, q_c0, q_c1 = QUADS[key]\n0362:         inp[q_r0 : q_r1 + 1, q_c0 : q_c1 + 1] = BG\n0363:         ar, ac = anchors[key]\n0364:         paste(inp, np.full((size, size), RED, dtype=int), ar, ac)\n0365: \n0366:     return inp if np.array_equal(main(inp), out) else None\n0367: \n0368: \n0369: def generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n0370:     for _ in range(MAX_RETRIES):\n0371:         grid = _gen_attempt()\n0372:         if grid is not None:\n0373:             return grid\n0374:     raise RuntimeError(\"failed to generate a valid b10624e5 input\")\n===== /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/7/prompt.md =====\n你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n\n每个参考题描述包含：\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n\n参考题目如下：\n<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"d749d46f\" lines=\"32-51\">\n<description>\nPack each solid foreground rectangle twice: wide across the top and tall from the bottom.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid has one background color and one foreground color; the foreground forms\nseparate solid rectangles, ordered from left to right.\n\nRule\nBuild a 10-row background canvas whose width is the packed width of the wide\nversions of the rectangles. For each source rectangle, paint a top-aligned\nrectangle of shape min(h,w) by max(h,w), with one background column between\nconsecutive rectangles. Then, starting again from the left edge, paint a\nbottom-aligned rectangle of shape max(h,w) by min(h,w) for each source rectangle,\nagain separated by one background column.\n\nKey insight\nThe input rectangles are not copied in their original orientations; each object\ncontributes one horizontal-facing and one vertical-facing normalized rectangle,\npreserving left-to-right object order.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"247ef758\" lines=\"35-46\">\n<description>\nMove colored sprites from the left strip into a framed area at marker-defined targets.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg background; rectangular frame on right with colored markers on its edges; sprites in a narrow left strip separated by a constant-color divider column.\n\nRule:\n- For each color, target rows/cols are where both opposite frame edges share that color. Targets are the Cartesian product.\n- Erase each sprite from the left and stamp it centered at every target. Higher sprites cover lower ones.\n\nKey insight: One sprite replicates to a grid of row × column marker intersections.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"c3fa4749\" lines=\"79-96\">\n<description>\nRecolor each side-marked multicolor object embedded in a monochrome panel to its marker color.\n\nInput structure:\n- Same-color 4-connected components form monochrome panel regions.\n- The bounding box of a panel may contain 4-connected non-panel-color objects.\n- A target object touches exactly one side of its panel bbox, and all of its\n  pixels on that side have one marker color.\n\nRule:\n- For every target object, fill any panel-colored holes enclosed by the object.\n- Recolor the object and filled holes to the side marker color.\n- Leave all other pixels unchanged.\n\nKey insight:\n- A multicolor object's single contact side identifies both which object should\n  be normalized and which color should replace it.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"880c1354\" lines=\"14-28\">\n<description>\nRecolor the separated outer regions by rotating their colors one step clockwise around the yellow-orange divider.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid contains a fixed yellow/orange divider structure.\n- All other colors form separated 4-connected monochrome regions around that divider.\n\nRule:\n- Leave the yellow and orange pixels unchanged.\n- Sort the non-divider regions by their centroid angle around the divider centroid in screen-coordinate clockwise order.\n- Each region keeps its cells and receives the color of the previous region in that cyclic order.\n\nKey insight:\n- The objects do not move; only the color labels cycle through the spatial order of the regions around the divider.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"dc46ea44\" lines=\"11-25\">\n<description>\nMove the lower sprite and its pink guide into the upper panel, aligning the sprite to the guide's lower-left branch.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has one dominant background color and one full-width separator row.\n- Below the separator are exactly two foreground roles: a five-pixel guide marker and one monochrome sprite.\n- The guide marker has normalized shape {(0,2), (1,2), (2,0), (2,2), (3,1)} and starts immediately below the separator.\n\nRule\n- Clear the canvas to the background, preserving the separator row.\n- Translate the guide marker upward so its top row becomes row 0.\n- Move the sprite, preserving its color and shape, so the sprite bbox bottom-right aligns to the translated guide's lower-left branch.\n\nKey insight\n- The marker supplies the destination anchor: its lower-left branch cell is where the moved sprite's bbox bottom-right must land.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"abbfd121\" lines=\"56-74\">\n<description>\nRecover the repeating background pattern hidden under the largest solid rectangle.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid is covered by a small row/column periodic pattern.\n- Several non-pattern colors form solid rectangular foreground objects that\n  overwrite the pattern.\n- The requested\n===== /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/7/des.md =====\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将分隔面板中的同色精灵按其内部孔洞数量排序，然后按排序顺序重新排列到输出画布的指定位置。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - Grey 色的完整行将网格分为上下两个面板。\n  - 上面板包含 3-5 个等大的单色矩形精灵（各使用不同颜色），排成一行，间隔一像素。每个精灵内部可能包含 0-3 个背景色孔洞。\n  - 下面板为空白（全背景色）。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对上面板的每个精灵，计算其内部 4-连通背景孔洞的数量。\n  - 按孔洞数量从少到多排序精灵。孔洞数量相同则保持原始从左到右顺序。\n  - 在下面板中，按排序后的顺序从左到右排列精灵，保持间隔一像素、顶部对齐。\n  - 清除上面板的精灵为背景色。保持 Grey 分隔行不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：孔洞数量是排序键，而非精灵的颜色或原始位置；解题者需要先发现孔洞计数规律，再理解重排列机制。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：每个前景对象作为\"印章\"，其像素数量决定了印章在输出中被重复盖印的次数，排成一行。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Azure。\n  - 网格中有 2-4 个 4-连通单色前景对象（使用不同颜色），每个对象面积为 2-5 像素。\n  - 对象之间不接触，且彼此分隔。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 创建一个新的背景色画布。\n  - 对每个对象，裁剪其 bbox 作为一个印章模板。\n  - 按对象在原始网格中从左到右的顺序处理。\n  - 对每个印章，将其连续盖印 N 次（N = 该对象的像素数量），从左到右排列，印章之间紧密相邻无间隔。\n  - 不同对象的印章组之间间隔两列背景色。\n  - 所有印章底部对齐。\n\n- `Key insight`：对象面积同时充当两个角色——它既定义了印章的形状，也定义了重复次数；解题者需要发现这种\"自引用\"关系。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：在网格中找到与隐含的周期性图案不一致的\"错误\"像素，将错误像素标记为特殊颜色。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 网格由一个小的 2x2 或 3x3 彩色 tile 周期性平铺而成，覆盖整个网格。\n  - 平铺中有少数像素（1-5 个）被人为修改为其他颜色，破坏了周期性。\n  - 修改后的颜色也是网格中已使用的颜色之一（即不能通过\"网格中未使用的颜色\"来识别错误）。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 推断出最小重复 tile 的尺寸和内容（通过多数投票：对每个 tile 位置取最常见的颜色）。\n  - 找到与推断 tile 不一致的像素位置。\n  - 将这些不一致的像素重着色为 Magenta（该颜色在原始输入中不存在）。\n  - 保持其他所有像素不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：错误像素无法通过颜色识别（它们使用的是合法颜色），只能通过位置在周期 tile 中的不一致来检测；推断 tile 本身就是一层非平凡的推理。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将多个面板中的精灵按照其\"朝向\"（由精灵形状的不对称性决定）分组，每组精灵的朝向相同的排成一列输出。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格中散布着若干个相同大小（3x3 bbox）的单色精灵，每个精灵的形状在其 3x3 bbox 内是不对称的，具有明确的视觉\"朝向\"（如一个 L 形的开口朝上/下/左/右）。\n  - 精灵使用不同的颜色。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个精灵，确定其朝向：将精灵的归一化形状与四个旋转版本比较，朝向由其归一化后所属的旋转类别决定（上、右、下、左）。\n  - 将所有同朝向的精灵分为一组。\n  - 创建输出画布，每组占一列，组内精灵从上到下排列，保持原色，间隔一像素。\n  - 列的顺序为：朝上、朝右、朝下、朝左（从左到右），列之间间隔两像素。\n  - 如果某个朝向没有精灵，则跳过该列。\n\n- `Key insight`：精灵的颜色和位置都是干扰项，唯一的分组键是形状的旋转朝向；解题者需要先抽象出朝向概念，再发现列排列的固定顺序。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：在包含\"发送器\"和\"接收器\"的网格中，每个发送器通过其颜色匹配的接收器，将自身的形状以镜像方式投影到接收器的另一侧。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格中间有一条完整的 Grey 垂直分隔线。\n  - 分隔线左侧有若干 4-连通单色\"发送器\"对象，右侧有若干单像素\"接收器\"标记。\n  - 每个发送器的颜色与恰好一个接收器标记的颜色匹配。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个发送器-接收器颜色对：\n    - 裁剪发送器的 bbox 形状。\n    - 将形状水平镜像翻转。\n    - 将翻转后的形状以接收器标记为锚点（对齐到发送器中标记对应位置），绘制在分隔线右侧。\n  - 清除所有接收器标记像素。发送器和分隔线保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：接收器标记既是颜色匹配键，也是空间定位锚点；发送器的形状经过镜像后\"穿越\"分隔线出现在右侧——颜色配对和镜像投影是两层独立的推理。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
