yu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/2/code.py:316:    - Each sender emits its complementary 3x3 pattern to the opposite endpoint of its wire:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/20/code.py:37:  the old logic was “pick one donor and one receiver globally”.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/20/code.py:38:  The new logic is “partition the scene into 2-3 color-coded donor/receiver pairs, then\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/20/code.py:78:  examples: blue donors always fill red receivers, green donors fill yellow receivers,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/20/code.py:79:  and grey donors fill pink receivers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/20/code.py:80:- D15/0 is also visible because donor and receiver outlines differ within every pair.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/17/code.py:19:#   * slot-marker orders above [A,B,C] are [2,3,1], so slot C is the first receiver,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/17/code.py:20:#     slot A is the second receiver, slot B is the third receiver.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/17/code.py:21:#   * source-side targets next to [A,B,C] are [3,1,2], so the shape at A asks for receiver 3,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/17/code.py:22:#     the shape at B asks for receiver 1, the shape at C asks for receiver 2.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/17/code.py:81:#   * the top stacks scramble which physical slot is \"1st / 2nd / 3rd receiver\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/17/code.py:82:#   * the side dot columns scramble which source bar goes to receiver 1/2/3,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/30/code.py:23:  is the receiver, then transfer colors by centroid row/column rank.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/30/code.py:27:  green-outline `src` -> yellow-outline `dst`. The distractors reuse one of the receiver\n/home/lixinyu/snap/n